ouche at a court appearance for his  son boucher was the head of an elite  chapter of the hell's angels everyone  knew mambushi was a killer and he knew  everyone knew  he seemed to love it  quebec's biker war raged for eight years  more than 160 people were killed and it  made the man at the middle of it  infamous  bouchet led the nomads an elite chapter  of the hell's angels he got the nickname  mom because he was apparently like an  overbearing mother for a time he seemed  untouchable  he wasn't but when boucher was arrested  in 1997 he was already a household name  he wouldn't be behind bars for long and  his reputation was still growing  was put on trial for ordering the murder  of two prison guards the goal was to  destabilize the justice system  [Music]  he won the first round the jury in  bouche's original trial found him not  guilty  [Applause]  laughing wouldn't last  a second trial was ordered on appeal one  of the reasons jurors had been  intimidated bouche was found guilty the  second time around  he would spend the rest of his days in  prison but still plugged into organized  crime in fact still ordering murders in  2018 he had another 10 years tacked on  to a life sentence  now the reason boucher became what some  have called a folk here on quebec is  because most of the victims of the biker  war were criminals but not all  for journalists who covered those years  there are names of innocent victims that  are impossible to forget the prison  guards who were killed diane levine  the 11 year old boy playing in a park  killed when a jeep nearby was blown up  and eve albert the father of two gunned  down gassing up his car he was shot nine  times because he was mistaken for a  biker  if for a time boucher lived a life that  seemed to be above the law it didn't  last he spent his final two decades  locked up what did last is the pain he  caused  mike armstrong global news  montreal  and that is global national for this  monday night i'm tracy tong tonight'